    "q-341719": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341719",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Given that $y=(5{x}^{2}+2x)^{x}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(5{x}^{2}+2x)^{x-1}\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}}$+10{x}^{2}+2x)$",
      "worked_solution": "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(5{x}^{2}+2x)^{x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((5{x}^{2}+2x)^{x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5{x}^{2}+2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5{x}^{2}+2x)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5{x}^{2}+2x))+(x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5{x}^{2}+2x)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(5{x}^{2}+2x)+x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5{x}^{2}+2x}\\cdot (10x+2)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5{x}^{2}+2x)+\\frac{10{x}^{2}+2x}{5{x}^{2}+2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5{x}^{2}+2x)+\\frac{10{x}^{2}+2x}{5{x}^{2}+2x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(5{x}^{2}+2x)^{x}:$    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(5{x}^{2}+2x)^{x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5{x}^{2}+2x)+\\frac{10{x}^{2}+2x}{5{x}^{2}+2x}) \\\\  & =(5{x}^{2}+2x)^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{(5{x}^{2}+2x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5{x}^{2}+2x)}{5{x}^{2}+2x}+\\frac{10{x}^{2}+2x}{5{x}^{2}+2x}) \\\\  & =(5{x}^{2}+2x)^{x-1}\\cdot ((5{x}^{2}+2x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5{x}^{2}+2x)+10{x}^{2}+2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
