    "q-138809": {
      "dom_id": "step-q138809",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Consider the function $y=(\\sqrt{x})^{x}.$ Its derivative is given by \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}{(\\sqrt{x})}^{x}\\cdot g(x).\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(\\sqrt{x})^{x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((\\sqrt{x})^{x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{x})) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(x)^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{x}))+(x)\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{x}))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{x})+x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{x})+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{2}y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(\\sqrt{x})^{x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{x})^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-138809-a",
